# make loadbench LB_LADDER=scripts/loadbench.ladder (issues #36, #39; docs/loadbench.md).
# One line per change, in order: LABEL COMMIT [NAME=VALUE...]. COMMIT may be HEAD. Consecutive
# lines are one attribution row. @NCPU is the online CPU count. Two consecutive lines with the
# same binary are an A/A control: lbsummary.py takes the cell's noise floor from them.
#   base     AK2_TIMINGS phase log only (the load path of main at d396c75)
#   thp      2 MiB-aligned table + MADV_HUGEPAGE
#   fill     the Filler interface (a refactor: expected no change)
#   scan     mmscan.AppendMinimizers: the scanner loop over a whole sequence, state in locals
#   recycle  seqio.Recycle: input blocks reuse their memory. Measured and REJECTED: reverted at
#            the final commit (see its revert); the rung stays as the measurement.
#   rc       AppendMinimizers keeps the reverse complement incrementally. This rung's commit also
#            contains the merge of main a8b0c72 (and loadbench/doc-only commits), so recycle -> rc
#            is that merge plus the change.
#   matesize the second mate's block sized like the first; newline index presized
#   batch    chash.GetBatch: a read's lookups with their cache misses overlapped
#   final    the benchmarked commit: batch minus recycle (the revert), plus merges of main
#   final-aa the same commit again: the A/A control (noise floor)
# Pread streams stay at upstream's 8 (16 measured no gain: results/g2/20261006-091341-5d20b94,
# results/g2/20261006-100409-16bc8b0); were 16 ever adopted, upstream would get
# K2_DB_READ_THREADS=16 too.
base 666459f6991cc5b99f4e7cbc278aeff866c35d7b
thp c138ab7f99e20af7dba8dc222c5b49630e4a50fb
fill 9de50376abd84d6cc4255ad45bab03f032e46bbc
scan fed426300c38b9f39f62af75fd542e02df705e24
recycle 97fe7e67196841bebf28290afc1fa1743fde4cea
rc 8db28f03b0340808aedad1d05534949fcb44c631
matesize fd4eea8ce87566815330d76539cab2cf306c9e7c
batch 411d4b430c577c80d9041483ed8167b2738dd9bb
final HEAD
final-aa HEAD
